---
import Layout from "../../../layouts/Layout.astro";

const question = "What materials are used for dry lining?";
const answer = "The material list for a Maidstone dry lining job falls into four groups:\n\nPlasterboard (always BS EN 520 stamped on the board edge):\n\n- 12.5mm Type A — the everyday wall board\n- 12.5mm Type H — moisture-resistant, for kitchens, utility rooms, bathroom zones away from direct water\n- 12.5mm Type F — fire-rated (often the pink or red board), 30 or 60 minutes to BS 476\n- 12.5mm Type D — impact-resistant for corridors, stairwells, schools\n- 12.5mm Type I — enhanced acoustic (sometimes called SoundBloc or Silent Board)\n- 15mm upgrades — better impact and acoustic at the cost of weight\n- 9.5mm — ceilings and tight curves where 12.5mm won't bend\n- Insulated plasterboard — PIR (best thermal per mm), phenolic (marginal gain, more expensive), graphite EPS (cheapest, thicker)\n\nFraming:\n\n- Metal stud and track — British Gypsum Gypframe or Knauf, 50/70/92/146mm widths to BS 7364\n- Timber stud — CLS or regularised softwood for non-fire-rated partitions\n- Channels and angles — for independent stud linings and bulkheads\n\nFinishing consumables:\n\n- Drywall adhesive (factory-premix, gypsum-based) for dot-and-dab\n- Jointing compound — ready-mix for small jobs, powder for larger areas\n- Scrim tape for joint reinforcement\n- Corner beads — galvanised for crisp external corners, PVC for wet areas\n\nBranding matters for warranty. British Gypsum GypWall, Knauf, Lafarge (Saint-Gobain), and AMF/Rockfon publish tested system data — fire rating, acoustic rating, structural load — that we rely on for sign-off. Generic unbranded boards don't carry tested performance data, which is why Building Control rejects them on fire-rated and acoustic jobs.\n\nMost boards and metal sections are ex-stock at Travis Perkins Maidstone, CCF Maidstone, or Selco Maidstone with next-day delivery; specialist acoustic and fire-rated boards usually take 24–48 hours.";
const description = "The material list for a Maidstone dry lining job falls into four groups: Plasterboard (always BS EN 520 stamped on the board edge): - 12.5mm Type A — the";
const canonical = "/drylining-faq/what-materials-are-used-for-dry-lining/";
const has_pricing = false;

const schema = {"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What materials are used for dry lining?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The material list for a Maidstone dry lining job falls into four groups:  Plasterboard (always BS EN 520 stamped on the board edge):  - 12.5mm Type A — the everyday wall board - 12.5mm Type H — moisture-resistant, for kitchens, utility rooms, bathroom zones away from direct water - 12.5mm Type F — fire-rated (often the pink or red board), 30 or 60 minutes to BS 476 - 12.5mm Type D — impact-resistant for corridors, stairwells, schools - 12.5mm Type I — enhanced acoustic (sometimes called SoundBloc or Silent Board) - 15mm upgrades — better impact and acoustic at the cost of weight - 9.5mm — ceilings and tight curves where 12.5mm won't bend - Insulated plasterboard — PIR (best thermal per mm), phenolic (marginal gain, more expensive), graphite EPS (cheapest, thicker)  Framing:  - Metal stud and track — British Gypsum Gypframe or Knauf, 50/70/92/146mm widths to BS 7364 - Timber stud — CLS or regularised softwood for non-fire-rated partitions - Channels and angles — for independent stud linings and bulkheads  Finishing consumables:  - Drywall adhesive (factory-premix, gypsum-based) for dot-and-dab - Jointing compound — ready-mix for small jobs, powder for larger areas - Scrim tape for joint reinforcement - Corner beads — galvanised for crisp external corners, PVC for wet areas  Branding matters for warranty. British Gypsum GypWall, Knauf, Lafarge (Saint-Gobain), and AMF/Rockfon publish tested system data — fire rating, acoustic rating, structural load — that we rely on for sign-off. Generic unbranded boards don't carry tested performance data, which is why Building Control rejects them on fire-rated and acoustic jobs.  Most boards and metal sections are ex-stock at Travis Perkins Maidstone, CCF Maidstone, or Selco Maidstone with next-day delivery; specialist acoustic and fire-rated boards usually take 24–48 hours."}}]},{"@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://dryliningmaidstone.co.uk/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"FAQ","item":"https://dryliningmaidstone.co.uk/faq/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":3,"name":"What materials are used for dry lining?","item":"https://dryliningmaidstone.co.uk/drylining-faq/what-materials-are-used-for-dry-lining/"}]}]};
---

<Layout
  title={`${question} | Drylining Maidstone`}
  description={description}
  canonical={canonical}
  schema={schema}
>
  <!-- HERO — matches new site design: dark navy gradient + yellow accent + breadcrumb + badge + H1 + CTAs -->
  <section style="position:relative;min-height:380px;display:flex;align-items:center;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#0a0e1a 0%,#1a1f3a 100%);overflow:hidden;">
    <img src="/images/maidstone-town.jpg" alt="Maidstone town centre — backdrop for the Drylining Maidstone FAQ" style="position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;opacity:0.20;" />
    <div style="position:absolute;inset:0;background:linear-gradient(135deg,rgba(10,14,26,0.88) 0%,rgba(26,31,58,0.88) 100%);"></div>
    <div class="container" style="position:relative;z-index:1;">
      <nav style="font-size:0.75rem;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.6);margin-bottom:1.25rem;">
        <a href="/" style="color:#FACC15;">HOME</a> / <a href="/faq/" style="color:#FACC15;">FAQ</a> / <span style="color:#FACC15;font-weight:600;">{question.slice(0, 60)}{question.length > 60 ? "…" : ""}</span>
      </nav>
      <span style="display:inline-block;padding:0.375rem 1rem;background:rgba(30,64,175,0.15);border:1px solid #FACC15;color:#FACC15;font-size:0.75rem;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.05em;border-radius:99px;margin-bottom:1.25rem;">MAIDSTONE DRYLINING FAQ</span>
      <h1 style="font-size:clamp(1.75rem,4vw,3rem);font-weight:800;color:var(--white);line-height:1.15;margin-bottom:1rem;max-width:48rem;">{question}</h1>
      <p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.85);margin-bottom:1.5rem;max-width:42rem;">Maidstone-specific answer with current 2026 pricing, building regulations, HMO licensing rules and practical advice from our local team.</p>
      <div style="display:flex;gap:1rem;flex-wrap:wrap;">
        <a href="/get-quote/" class="btn btn-highlight">Get My Free Quote</a>
        <a href="/faq/" class="btn btn-outline" style="color:var(--white);border-color:rgba(255,255,255,0.3);">All FAQs</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <main class="container" style="padding:3rem 1.5rem 4rem;">
    <article class="card" style="padding:2rem;max-width:880px;">
      <div style="background:rgba(30,64,175,0.05);border-left:4px solid #FACC15;padding:1rem 1.5rem;margin-bottom:1.75rem;border-radius:0 8px 8px 0;">
        <p style="margin:0;font-size:0.875rem;color:var(--text);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.05em;font-weight:700;">Quick Answer</p>
        <p style="margin:0.5rem 0 0;font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.7;font-weight:500;">{description}</p>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-answer" style="font-size:1.0625rem;line-height:1.85;color:var(--text);">
  <p style="margin:0 0 1.1rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;">The material list for a Maidstone dry lining job falls into four groups:</p>
  <p style="margin:0 0 1.1rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;">Plasterboard (always BS EN 520 stamped on the board edge):</p>
  <ul style="list-style:disc;padding-left:1.5rem;margin:0 0 1.25rem;color:var(--text);">
    <li style="margin-bottom:0.45rem;line-height:1.75;">12.5mm Type A — the everyday wall board</li>
    <li style="margin-bottom:0.45rem;line-height:1.75;">12.5mm Type H — moisture-resistant, for kitchens, utility rooms, bathroom zones away from direct water</li>
    <li style="margin-bottom:0.45rem;line-height:1.75;">12.5mm Type F — fire-rated (often the pink or red board), 30 or 60 minutes to BS 476</li>
    <li style="margin-bottom:0.45rem;line-height:1.75;">12.5mm Type D — impact-resistant for corridors, stairwells, schools</li>
    <li style="margin-bottom:0.45rem;line-height:1.75;">12.5mm Type I — enhanced acoustic (sometimes called SoundBloc or Silent Board)</li>
    <li style="margin-bottom:0.45rem;line-height:1.75;">15mm upgrades — better impact and acoustic at the cost of weight</li>
    <li style="margin-bottom:0.45rem;line-height:1.75;">9.5mm — ceilings and tight curves where 12.5mm won't bend</li>
    <li style="margin-bottom:0.45rem;line-height:1.75;">Insulated plasterboard — PIR (best thermal per mm), phenolic (marginal gain, more expensive), graphite EPS (cheapest, thicker)</li>
  </ul>
  <p style="margin:0 0 1.1rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;">Framing:</p>
  <ul style="list-style:disc;padding-left:1.5rem;margin:0 0 1.25rem;color:var(--text);">
    <li style="margin-bottom:0.45rem;line-height:1.75;">Metal stud and track — British Gypsum Gypframe or Knauf, 50/70/92/146mm widths to BS 7364</li>
    <li style="margin-bottom:0.45rem;line-height:1.75;">Timber stud — CLS or regularised softwood for non-fire-rated partitions</li>
    <li style="margin-bottom:0.45rem;line-height:1.75;">Channels and angles — for independent stud linings and bulkheads</li>
  </ul>
  <p style="margin:0 0 1.1rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;">Finishing consumables:</p>
  <ul style="list-style:disc;padding-left:1.5rem;margin:0 0 1.25rem;color:var(--text);">
    <li style="margin-bottom:0.45rem;line-height:1.75;">Drywall adhesive (factory-premix, gypsum-based) for dot-and-dab</li>
    <li style="margin-bottom:0.45rem;line-height:1.75;">Jointing compound — ready-mix for small jobs, powder for larger areas</li>
    <li style="margin-bottom:0.45rem;line-height:1.75;">Scrim tape for joint reinforcement</li>
    <li style="margin-bottom:0.45rem;line-height:1.75;">Corner beads — galvanised for crisp external corners, PVC for wet areas</li>
  </ul>
  <p style="margin:0 0 1.1rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;">Branding matters for warranty. British Gypsum GypWall, Knauf, Lafarge (Saint-Gobain), and AMF/Rockfon publish tested system data — fire rating, acoustic rating, structural load — that we rely on for sign-off. Generic unbranded boards don't carry tested performance data, which is why Building Control rejects them on fire-rated and acoustic jobs.</p>
  <p style="margin:0 0 1.1rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;">Most boards and metal sections are ex-stock at Travis Perkins Maidstone, CCF Maidstone, or Selco Maidstone with next-day delivery; specialist acoustic and fire-rated boards usually take 24–48 hours.</p>
      </div>

      {has_pricing && (
        <div style="margin-top:2rem;padding:1.25rem 1.5rem;background:#fef3c7;border-left:4px solid #f59e0b;border-radius:0 8px 8px 0;">
          <p style="margin:0;font-size:0.875rem;font-weight:700;color:#92400e;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.05em;">Pricing & figures — read this</p>
          <p style="margin:0.5rem 0 0;font-size:0.9375rem;color:#78350f;line-height:1.7;">Any prices, fees or figure-based guidance on this page are indicative and intended for budget planning only. They are not a quote and not a substitute for the published source. For current fees always check: <strong>Maidstone Borough Council Building Control fee schedule</strong>, <strong>Maidstone Borough Council HMO licensing fees</strong>, <strong>BCIS construction cost indices</strong>, and the <strong>current Approved Documents</strong> (free PDFs from GOV.UK). Send us your plans and we will turn around a fixed-price written quote within 48 hours.</p>
        </div>
      )}

      <div style="margin-top:2.5rem;padding:1.5rem;background:var(--accent);border-radius:var(--radius);">
        <h3 style="font-size:1.25rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin-bottom:0.75rem;">Need a quote for this in Maidstone?</h3>
        <p style="color:var(--text);margin-bottom:1.25rem;font-size:1rem;">Send a brief, your plans or just a few photos. We will turn around a fixed-price quote within 48 hours, anywhere across ME14–ME20, TN12 and TN27 postcodes.</p>
        <div style="display:flex;gap:0.75rem;flex-wrap:wrap;">
